  "variance_model": "the per-contrast paired form, which is HB's two-arm reduction (analysis-model DRAFT A.2-A.5, A.12): V = V_seed + V_prompt; V_seed = s_d^2 / J with s_d^2 the sample variance (ddof 1) of the J seed differences, df_seed = J - 1; V_prompt = max(0, MS_P - MS_E) / (P J) x 10^4 from the two-way analysis of variance of the J x P table D(j, p) = y(a0, j, p) - y(m, j, p) (MS_P on P - 1 df, MS_E on (P - 1)(J - 1) df); Satterthwaite df = V^2 / (V_seed^2 / df_seed + q), q = (MS_P / (P J) x 10^4)^2 / (P - 1) + (MS_E / (P J) x 10^4)^2 / ((P - 1)(J - 1)) when MS_P > MS_E, else q = 0",
